  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added line-level discount support to the invoice system:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **errors.js**: Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code for validation failures\n\n2. **invoices.js**:\n   - `createInvoice`: Now accepts `discountPercent` in line input (0-100, decimals allowed). Defaults to 0 if omitted. Stored on each line.\n   - `addLine`: Same validation as `createInvoice` for new lines\n   - `invoiceTotals`: Updated to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n     - `subtotal` = sum of line totals (qty \u00d7 unitPrice)\n     - `discount` = sum of (line total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100) \n     - `total` = subtotal - discount\n     - All amounts clamped at 0\n\n3. **tests**: Added 16 new tests covering:\n   - Valid discount percentages (0, 10, 12.5, 100)\n   - Invalid inputs (negative, >100, non-numbers)\n   - Default to 0 when omitted\n   - Discount calculations with single and multiple lines\n   - Clamping behavior\n   - Error handling in `addLine`\n\nThe implementation properly validates discount percentages and ensures no computed amount goes below zero.",
